Hunch Home: listening with no wake word (experimental, off by default)

The speech model
----------------
When the owner first switches listening on and confirms it, Hunch Home fetches one speech model into its data
folder. It is not in this image.

  Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2, by NVIDIA
  https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  Fetched in the 8-bit ONNX form published by the sherpa-onnx project (k2-fsa):
  https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/download/asr-models/sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-int8.tar.bz2
  That form is NVIDIA's model converted to ONNX and quantised to 8 bits by sherpa-onnx. The archive is checked
  against a SHA-256 pinned in hunch_app/listen/speech.py before it is used.

The libraries in this image that listening uses
-----------------------------------------------
  sherpa-onnx and sherpa-onnx-core (speech-to-text runtime), by the k2-fsa project. Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx

  pysilero-vad (the speech detector), by Michael Hansen, with the Silero VAD model by the Silero Team.
  MIT License. https://github.com/rhasspy/pysilero-vad and https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad

  parec (pulseaudio-utils) and arecord (alsa-utils), Debian's packages; their copyright files are in
  /usr/share/doc/pulseaudio-utils/ and /usr/share/doc/alsa-utils/.
